cc99d0f707768d9d94d0ac8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-31T17:31:39Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-31T17:31:39Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"message":"fix(cassandra): pin spring-ai-openai version + guard cypress entity patches on databaseTypeCassandra\n\nTwo changes that keep the base cassandra example green while making the cassandra generators safe\nto compose into the orchestrator''s assembled, multi-database blueprint:\n\n- cassandra-spring-boot: pin <version>2.0.0-M7</version> on the spring-ai-openai dependency. In the\n  orchestrator''s composition this editFile can run before <dependencyManagement> exists, so the BOM\n  anchor misses and the version is unresolved (\"''dependencies.dependency.version'' ... is missing\" →\n  BUILD FAILURE). An explicit version is robust to ordering and a harmless no-op for the standalone\n  example (where the BOM also lands).\n\n- cypress: guard POST_WRITING_ENTITIES on application.databaseTypeCassandra. These patches read the\n  Cassandra-only entity.primaryKeySaathratri metadata (composite-key URLs, MAP/SET/date-time widgets,\n  search form). No-op for the standalone cassandra example (all apps are Cassandra); essential once\n  this generator is copied into the orchestrator as the cypress override, where it also runs for SQL\n  services — the DB-agnostic navbar/entityItemSelector fix in POST_WRITING still applies to every app.\n\nLayer-1 snapshots green (12/12). Validated via the orchestrator one-shot: cassandra services build\n(216 ITs) and SQL services'' cypress navbar selector is fixed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dc29828a9eed51a988969fbdf284b6e2f3cd84fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/generator-jhipster-cassandra/git/trees/dc29828a9eed51a988969fbdf284b6e2f3cd84fc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/genera