iew_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/generator-jhipster-cassandra/commits/c87489910ac56c7d1df982aeddf99994b170ea39/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-28T20:29:44Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-28T20:29:44Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"message":"fix(cypress): lint cleanups for widget @Input and unsafe cy chains\n\nTwo ESLint regressions surfaced by the band-aid + regen iteration:\n\n  1. @typescript-eslint/no-inferrable-types: drop the `: string` annotation\n     from `@Input() fieldName: string = ''''` across the 5 widget components —\n     the empty-string literal already implies the type.\n\n  2. cypress/unsafe-to-chain-command: split `.clear().type(X)` and\n     `.type(X).blur()` into two statements in the cypress generator\n     passes (c.7 date-time smoke test, c.9 MAP<DAYJS> round-trip, c.10\n     edit-dialog tests, c.11 delete-row tests). Each command now has its\n     own `cy.get(...).<action>()` statement, satisfying the cypress\n     plugin''s chaining rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7ea654b8d15c0511931b9a5ffc22d0ce584eaeba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/generator-jhipster-cassandra/git/trees/7ea654b8d15c0511931b9a5ffc22d0ce584eaeba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/generator-jhipster-cassandra/git/commits/c87489910ac56c7d1df982aeddf99994b170ea39","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1010740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpa