hub.com/users/amarpatel-xx/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/commits/29745b87ae4d36537cba74dbd1209ed6ad84e8cf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-07T16:34:50Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-07T16:34:50Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"message":"fix(harness): bring up the docker stack in the e2e phase instead of pre-flight aborting\n\nsaathratri-run-all-tests.sh previously only CHECKED for Keycloak/Registry and\nskipped e2e when they weren''t running, requiring a manual deploy first — unlike\nthe ai-postgresql and orchestrator harnesses, which are self-contained. The e2e\nphase now starts Keycloak (gated on its OIDC endpoint, since the Registry does\neager OIDC discovery at boot and exits(1) if Keycloak isn''t serving), then the\nRegistry (gated on :8761), then each app''s Cassandra DB via docker:db:up.\n\nVerified: one-shot run from a cold machine — backends, frontends, and all three\ne2e suites green (incl. the embedding-lifecycle spec).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TsfLhC3Jrki6WmZckNGfSN","tree":{"sha":"c2fa786399310a6fdc0f914f2976c592fd0635bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/git/trees/c2fa786399310a6fdc0f914f2976c592fd0635bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/git/commits/29745b87ae4d36537cba74dbd1209ed6ad84e8cf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.github