atel-xx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/commits/37e4f005c4083647e55ba6e014e9bfe00d80c94a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-30T17:56:35Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-30T17:56:35Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"message":"test: add run-all-tests.sh one-shot harness (store e2e flake UNRESOLVED)\n\nSingle script: regen + backend + frontend + webapp build + backend launch +\nreadiness gate + e2e + teardown + report.\n\nHONEST STATUS — NOT yet a reliable one-shot. cassandrastore e2e fails on the\nfirst pass, and in the latest run the whole-suite retry ALSO failed with\n\"Cypress failed to verify that your server is running\" (localhost:8080 was\nunreachable by then) — pointing at backend instability over the long\nsequential run, not a Cypress timing flake. The gateway->remote route gate did\nNOT prevent it (route was 302/live at gate time), so that theory is disproven.\nThe script''s result-scraping also has a bug (reported store \"passed\" while exit\nwas 1). Flake + scraping bug both still open; root-causing next.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a53e67eed609c08582b795bfbf5948b06d258f45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/git/trees/a53e67eed609c08582b795bfbf5948b06d258f45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/git/commits/37e4f005c4083647e55ba6e014e9bfe00d80c94a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1010740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.githu