mail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-28T19:00:14Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"message":"feat(cypress): MAP/SET round-trip tests for 5 example entities (band-aid)\n\nHand-crafted `should round-trip MAP/SET widget entries through POST` test\nper affected entity:\n\n- add-ons-available-by-organization.cy.ts: MAP<TEXT>, MAP<DECIMAL>, MAP<BOOLEAN>\n- add-ons-selected-by-organization.cy.ts: same 3 MAP variants\n- landing-page-by-organization.cy.ts: same 3 MAP variants\n- saathratri-entity-3.cy.ts: SET<TEXT>\n- set-entity-by-organization.cy.ts: SET<TEXT>\n\nEach test fills required composite-key/scalar fields with distinct sample\nvalues (suffix 010/020/030/040/050 to avoid collision with the create-\ninstance variant), exercises each widget''s Add row via the data-cy hooks\nadded in 37f2d61, clicks Save, and asserts the POST response body contains\nthe widget entries.\n\nMAP<DAYJS> (addOnDetailsBigInt, detailsBigInt) is excluded — the nested\n<app-date-time> inside the Add row needs more elaborate interaction than\ncurrent scope allows. Smoke test (-add-key + -add-button reachable) still\ncovers it.\n\nPermanent fix lives in generator-jhipster-cassandra cypress/generator.js\nPOST_WRITING_ENTITIES (c.9).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6b98e4e8bba09d4ffaf6f028f21a0bd232292c69","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/git/trees/6b98e4e8bba09d4ffaf6f028f21a0bd232292c69"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/git/commits/82825dde39bacd6ee7068da9440d137e9daf1e49","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1010740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amar