ner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/commits/277a41c4a4d98b09f78ebf828d4fcee5fae680af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-28T16:14:29Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-28T16:14:29Z","email":"amarppatel1@gmail.com","name":"Amar Premsaran Patel"},"message":"chore(deploy): open each service in a Windows Terminal tab on Windows\n\nThe .sh version already opens each service in a tab via ttab; the .bat\nversion used `start \"Name\" mvnw.cmd ...` which opens a SEPARATE console\nwindow per service — cluttering the desktop and hard to flip between.\n\nSwitch to `wt -w 0 new-tab --title \"...\" -d \"%cd%\" cmd /k ...` so each\nservice (Keycloak / JHipster Registry / Gateway / Blog / Store) opens as\na new tab in the current Windows Terminal window. `-d \"%cd%\"` preserves\nthe working directory so mvnw.cmd resolves; `cmd /k` keeps the tab open\nif the server crashes so the error is visible.\n\nRequires Windows Terminal (wt.exe) — installed by default on Windows 11.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e65d8cff94820d9fd7fd247c20378f8f82f4cc8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/git/trees/e65d8cff94820d9fd7fd247c20378f8f82f4cc8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/saathratri/jhipster-cassandra-example/git/commits/277a41c4a4d98b09f78ebf828d4fcee5fae680af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1010740?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/amarpatel-xx/followers"