,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTc2NDA1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nickmisasi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/okrbest/okrbest/commits/5c261425844d2d73d8d486436b340d750538ebfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T16:11:21Z","email":"nick.misasi@mattermost.com","name":"Nick Misasi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T04:57:04Z","email":"76608088+sinyebin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"sinyebin"},"message":"MM-70071: Automatically select hosted push notification server based on license (#37802)\n\n* MM-70071: Automatically select hosted push notification server based on license\n\nCo-authored-by: nick.misasi <nick.misasi@mattermost.com>\n\n* test: fix mock-store fallout from push endpoint license listener\n\nCo-authored-by: nick.misasi <nick.misasi@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70071: address review feedback on push endpoint sync\n\nCo-authored-by: nick.misasi <nick.misasi@mattermost.com>\n\n* ci: retrigger enterprise tests against updated companion branch\n\nCo-authored-by: nick.misasi <nick.misasi@mattermost.com>\n\n* ci: retrigger flaky artifact build\n\nCo-authored-by: nick.misasi <nick.misasi@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70071: revert any hosted push endpoint to test on entitlement loss\n\nCo-authored-by: nick.misasi <nick.misasi@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70071: add nil-safe License.HasMHPNS entitlement check\n\nCo-authored-by: nick.misasi <nick.misasi@mattermost.com>\n\n* MM-70071: drop preview-tree docs for auto-selected push server\n\nMonorepo MDX is still unpublished; this belongs in mattermost/docs.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* MM-70071: stub InitEmailBatching on guest-invite email mocks\n\nLicense teardown now SaveConfigs the push endpoint, which fires the existing email-batching config listener.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n* MM-70071: don''t re-init email batching on push-server license sync\n\nLicense teardown SaveConfigs the push endpoint, which fired the existing\nemail-batching listener and panicked tests that mock EmailService.\nRe-init batching only when EnableEmailBatching changes, and stub the\nremaining invite mock used during helper cleanup.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nick13misasi@gmail.com>\n\n* MM-70071: re-init email batching when the interval setting changes\n\nKeep EmailBatchingInterval live at runtime; only ignore unrelated\nconfig writes such as the push-server license sync.\n\nCo-authored-by: Nick Misasi <nick13misasi@gmail.com>\n\n* MM-70071: isolate mock tests from push endpoint sync\n\nUse custom push endpoints in shared mock fixtures so unrelated tests do not need config-listener expectations.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mattermost Build <build@mattermost.com>\n(cherry picked from commit 62056e5a7c6c817fe95e4edeaeee8af8fb6b0b7d)\n\nUpstream: https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/62056e5a7c6c817fe95e4edeaeee8af8fb6b0b7d","tree":{"sha":"20a71a61a4415df50eb44bd466e93a3b5ef4807a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/okrbest/okrbest/git/trees/20a71a61a4415df50eb44bd466e93a3b5ef4807a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/okrbest/okrbest/git/commits/5c261425844d2d73d8d486436b340d750538ebfb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76608088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sinyebin","id":76608088,"login":"sinyebin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NjA4MDg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/okrbest/okrbest/commit/5c261425844d2d73d8d486436b340d750538ebfb","node_id":"C_kwDOOUH-iNoAKDVjMjYxNDI1ODQ0ZDJkNzNkOGQ0ODY0MzZiMzQwZDc1MDUzOGViZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/okrbest/okrbest/commit/34711e04f75e536a816b4fe18a8cee2d4db050b3","sha":"34711e04f75e536a816b4fe18a8cee2d4db050b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/okrbest/okrbest/commits/34711e04f75e536a816b4fe18a8cee2d4db050b3"}],"sha":"5c261425844d2d73d8d486436b340d750538ebfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/okrbest/okrbest/commits/5c261425844d2d73d8d486436b340d750538ebfb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1210556?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/cursor","id":206951365,"login":"cursor[bot]","node_id":"BOT_kgDODFXTxQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cursor%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/okrbest/okrbest/commits/34711e04f75e536a816b4fe18a8cee2d4db050b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T14:30:34Z","email":"206951365+cursor[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"cursor[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-08T04:57:04Z","email":"76608088+sinyebin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"sinyebin"},"message":"[MM-70198] Fix post preview layout shift by overlaying the \"Show more\" control (#37974)\n\n* [MM-70198] Overlay permalink preview \"Show more\" to avoid layout shift\n\nPost permalink previews clip tall content and reveal a \"Show more\"\naffordance only after the body is measured on mount. The ellipsis-style\nbutton was rendered in normal flow below the clipped text, so when it\nflashed in the preview grew taller and pushed following content down.\n\nPosition the ellipsis \"Show more\" button absolutely over the faded bottom\nof the preview so it is revealed without changing the preview''s height.\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* [MM-70198] Satisfy stylelint property order\n\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\n\n* Change fade out to use a mask-image so colours match\n\n* Change new post preview fade out to fully fade before toggle text\n\n* Add E2E test for post preview Show more layout shift\n\nVerify that the overflowing permalink preview ''Show more'' control is\noverlaid on the preview and does not change the post height when it is\nrevealed after mount.\n\n* Move new E2E test to match format of others\n\n* Address PR feedback: extend permalink preview fade transparent stop to 24px\n\nmatthewbirtch suggested moving the mask-image fully-transparent stop from\ncalc(100% - 18px) to calc(100% - 24px). Applied to both the -webkit-mask-image\nand mask-image declarations to keep them consistent.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>\nCo-authored-by: mattermost-code <matty-code@mattermost.com>\nCo-authored-by: Harrison Healey <harrisonmhealey@gmail.com>\n(cherry picked from commit c36f979edd0ec3912097c4ffcd944e3f09fb67cd)\n\nUpstream: https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost/commit/c36f979edd0ec3912097c4ffcd944e3f09fb67cd","tree":{"sha":"47634165460b8d70c53585c88817e183cd5454d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/okrbest/okrbest/git/trees/47634165460b8d70c53585c88817e183cd5454d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/okrbest/okrbest/git/commits/34711e04f75e536a816b4fe18a8cee2d4db050b3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/76608088?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sinyebin","id":76608088,"login":"sinyebin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NjA4MDg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sinyebin","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/okrbest/okrbest/commit/34711e04f75e536a816b4fe18a8c